  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1229 AM CDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nWhile temperatures on Tuesday for most of the Panhandles are still \nexpected to be on the hot side (exception will be the northwest), we \nshould be on a transition track as a cold front is expected to \nexpand down through most of the Panhandles, the southeast being the \nexception.  Along and behind the front we expect a medium to high \nchance of showers and storms (40-70%).  On Wednesday that front may \nretreat northwest a bit, leading to the main area of precipitation \nbeing along and northwest of the Hereford to Perryton line.  Over \nthe course of the rest of the week and into the weekend the ridge \nwill gradually break down and we could have multiple days of showers \nand storms with cooler, more seasonable highs as a more zonal flow \nto slightly northwest flow comes into play.  Highs on Friday and \nSaturday could be widespread low to mid 80s, which is certainly a \nbreak from the past couple of months well above normal temperatures \non a daily basis. \n\nWeber",
